 who doesn't really like what he's  doing but remains desperate to find a  cure for the sick  despite all this awfulness there is a  silver lining  gus seems quite happy to find other  hybrids and his ability to speak  saves him from the scalpel besides a  cliffhanger at the end of the episode  makes it pretty clear that amy and  shepard are gearing up for the mother of  all daring rescue operations  speaking of shepard the season finale is  called big man and sure enough it puts  tommy jeopard and his past trauma front  and  center through a combination of  flashbacks and expository dialogue we  learned that when his wife gave birth  amidst the apocalyptic chaos  jeopard panicked and ran away from her  and their child when he saw that the  baby was a human sheep hybrid  he never found either of them again and  his cowardice and  loss weigh heavily on him as such part  of his decision to help gus is an  attempt to redeem his past mistakes  i wasn't afraid of him  i was afraid of me it's all very tragic  and gets even more so when the last men  ruin the moment by shooting shepard  fortunately amy is able to rescue him  before he succumbs to the injury  like everyone else who's not affiliated  with the last men and general abbott's  nefarious plot to use a cure for the  sick to grab  even more power bear has a battled time  in the ending of sweet tooth season one  in her case though it's mainly because  viewers find out how awful her life has  been  as with jeppard we learn a whole bunch  of her backstory starting with her real  name  becky walker and the reason she ended up  with the animal army  bear lost her parents to the sick had  her hybrid little sister taken away and  wandered around until she met tiger and  started her new life  fortunately the audience learns that  wendy is bear's long-lost sister so  there's hope for happiness yet  bear is also responsible for the final  reveal of the season when her attempts  to tinker with a satellite phone finally  connect her to a station in alaska  where a very surprised birdie answers  the phone with gus's mother still alive  it's pretty clear that the potential  sweet tooth season 2 just gained a very  powerful and determined player  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

